---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How Tucson Web Development handles the information you send through this site.">
  <article class="wrap py-16">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <div class="prose-twd measure mt-8">
      <p><em>Last updated November 19, 2026</em></p>
      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the contact form, I receive the name, email, phone number, website, and message you enter. This site
        doesn't use advertising trackers or sell any information.
      </p>
      <h2>How I use it</h2>
      <p>
        Only to reply to you and to work on your project. If you check the text-message box, I may text you about your
        project. Reply STOP at any time to opt out. I never share your phone number for marketing.
      </p>
      <h2>The chat assistant</h2>
      <p>
        Messages you type into the chat bubble are sent to Anthropic, which runs the AI model, to generate a reply. The
        site doesn't save your chat or ask for your name, and closing the page clears it. Please don't type anything
        private into the chat. To limit abuse, the server keeps a scrambled (hashed) version of your IP address for up to
        an hour.
      </p>
      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>Messages are kept in my business email for as long as they're useful for your project, and you can ask me to delete them at any time.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
